    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0416" n="410" sameAs="frus:frus1942v02/pg410"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 (E. W.)/11–742: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Admiral William D. Leahy, Chief of Staff to the
                        Commander in Chief of the Army and Navy, to the Consul General at Algiers
                        (Cole)</hi><anchor n="16" xml:id="d414-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-31">October 31, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>No. M–26. For Murphy. Please advise Flagpole that we consider it highly desirable
                    that French commanders be given instructions on D day that incidents on the part
                    of the Spanish, however provocative, should not be permitted to lead to
                    retaliatory action on the part of the French until after the consolidation of
                    the American forces on shore.</p>
                <p>Eisenhower is requesting British to make similar representations to France on D
                    day.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Leahy</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d414-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d414-f1-content">
                <p>Copy supplied by the Office of the Secretary of Defense under cover of letter of
                    September 7, 1960.</p>
            </note>
